# CONFENGE redirects — canonical manifest consumed by the Netcup/nginx renderer;
# the legacy preview also reads the same publish-root file. Production authority
# remains nginx/Netcup. Do not add trailing-slash-only rules: the renderers
# normalize them, so one rule covers both /path and /path/.

# --- Host canonization (force so existing files do not shadow) ---
https://confenge.netlify.app/*  https://confenge.com.br/:splat  301!

# --- File extension / legacy HTML ---
/privacidade.html  /privacidade/  301!

# --- Form success rewrites (pretty URLs, noindex pages) ---
/obrigado  /obrigado.html  200
/obrigado-contrato  /obrigado-contrato.html  200
/obrigado-edital  /obrigado-edital.html  200
/obrigado-operacao  /obrigado-operacao.html  200

# --- Live-intelligence shareable result (opaque random token, noindex) ---
# Deliberately NO rule here. `/analise-cnpj/r/` is a real static page and the
# opaque token travels as its `?t=` query, so the address resolves through the
# ordinary pretty-URL chain like every other page. A token-as-path-segment shape
# is not expressible in this contract: a wildcard source requires a one-to-one
# `:splat` in the target (HC_REDIRECT_SPLAT_UNSAFE), `:placeholder` sources are
# rejected (HC_REDIRECT_SELECTOR_UNSUPPORTED), destination query strings are
# rejected (HC_REDIRECT_TARGET_QUERY_UNSUPPORTED), and the runtime location
# allowlist is anchored at the function name, so a function-served token path
# cannot be routed either.

